    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "executeQuery",
        "query": "SELECT string_agg(t.table_name || '(' || t.cols || ')', E'\\n' ORDER BY t.table_name) AS schema\nFROM (SELECT c.table_name,\n             string_agg(c.column_name || ' ' || c.data_type, ', ' ORDER BY c.ordinal_position) AS cols\n      FROM information_schema.columns c\n      WHERE c.table_schema = 'public'\n      GROUP BY c.table_name) t;",
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
      "typeVersion": 2.6,
      "position": [
        -380,
        100
      ],
      "id": "e65163f9-06bc-5b6e-bfb2-85c1467d54c4",
      "name": "Analyst - Load schema",
      "credentials": {
        "postgres": {
          "id": "shopDbReadOnly01",
          "name": "Shop DB (read-only)"
        }
      },
      "executeOnce": true,
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 2
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// One place that holds the loop state: first pass comes from the router, retries come from \"Loop - Add critique\".\nconst prev = $input.first().json;\nreturn [{ json: {\n  question: prev.question ?? $('Config - Request').first().json.question,\n  schema: $('Analyst - Load schema').first().json.schema,\n  attempt: prev.attempt ?? 1,\n  critique: prev.critique ?? '',\n} }];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -160,
        100
      ],
      "id": "2dc30764-df67-5a31-a3f1-c03aaf5cf281",
      "name": "Loop - State"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ $json.critique ? 'Your previous answer was rejected by the reviewer: ' + $json.critique + '\\nQuery the database again and answer correctly.\\n\\n' : '' }}Question: {{ $json.question }}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=You are the data analyst of an online coffee and tea shop. You answer the owner's questions\nusing ONLY rows returned by the run_sql tool in this conversation.\n\nDATABASE (PostgreSQL), table(columns):\n{{ $json.schema }}\n\nBUSINESS RULES\n- Revenue counts only orders with status paid, shipped or delivered. Use the view order_totals for order revenue.\n- Line revenue is order_items.quantity * order_items.unit_price (not products.price).\n- Dates: orders.ordered_at is a timestamp; \"last month\" means the previous calendar month.\n\nHOW TO WORK\n1. Write one SELECT for the question and call run_sql. Never INSERT, UPDATE or DELETE.\n2. If run_sql returns an error, read it, fix the query and call run_sql again.\n3. Answer in 1-4 short sentences. Every number you write must be copied from the rows (you may round money to\n   whole euros). If the rows are empty, say that no data matched.\n4. Do not show SQL, table names or column names in the answer.\n5. The database holds only this shop's data. For benchmarks, market averages or anything outside it, say that\n   the data does not contain it. Never type such values into the SQL.\n",
          "maxIterations": 6,
          "returnIntermediateSteps": true
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        80,
        100
      ],
      "id": "25002b1a-40f0-5850-950d-83bed0dcb63e",
